WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.933
Here are two proteins modeled in NanoCoFold.
We'll install the app, run an analysis and find it in the database.

2
00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:19.475
Start on Ubuntu with your GPU listed by nvidia-smi.
Check the installation requirements in the GitHub README.

3
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.642
Open NanoCoFold_public on GitHub.
The video follows the Korean README. You can use the English one.

4
00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:33.975
Download the code with git clone. Run cd NanoCoFold_public.
You should see install.sh and start.sh in that folder.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:41.725
For the first complex, run bash install.sh --profile complex.
This installs Boltz-2 and Chai-1.

6
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:49.933
For all four modes and all engines, run bash install.sh --profile all.
Choose one install command for the analyses you want to run.

7
00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:57.392
Wait for the installation-complete message
before starting the web server.

8
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:05.517
Run bash start.sh --port 18765 and leave the terminal open.
Open the NanoCoFold address printed in the terminal in your browser.

9
00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:16.808
In Environment & setup, choose your analysis and check the environment.
When the check finishes, click Prepare analysis.

10
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:25.850
Once the required checks pass, click Prepare analysis.
You can now set up the protein prediction.

11
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:37.850
Load the public example to enter one copy each of Barnase and Barstar.
For your own FASTA, enter >name, then the sequence on the next line.

12
00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:48.267
Check for Boltz-2, no MSA, seed 42 and one planned model.
If Run analysis is disabled, click Go to environment check.

13
00:01:48.292 --> 00:02:00.642
Here we use CPU practice mode in Compare existing nanobodies.
Click Run analysis once. Follow its progress in Jobs & logs.

14
00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:10.725
This saved GPU run took about 57 seconds. One model succeeded, none failed.
Click Open results to see its report.

15
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:20.725
The two input sequences produced one model.
Rotate the 3D structure to see where the two colored chains meet.

16
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:30.975
PAE estimates the error in the relative positions of residues, in Å.
Use the color scale to read the regions on either side of the chain boundary.

17
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:43.267
Whole-complex ipTM is 0.078 and mean interface PAE is 24.84 Å.
The run finished with low confidence in the chains' relative positions.

18
00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:52.767
Choose Design new nanobodies and load the public IL-6 example.
New candidates are generated from a target sequence or structure.

19
00:02:52.792 --> 00:03:04.558
One backbone per generator gives two candidates. Four engines can produce eight models.
For public MSA, allow the app to send the example sequences.

20
00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:14.892
This run evaluated eight models from two candidates.
Neither candidate passed final selection.

21
00:03:14.917 --> 00:03:23.433
In section 04, check exclusions by criterion, including ipSAE and ipTM.
A single model can have more than one reason for exclusion.

22
00:03:23.458 --> 00:03:33.850
In Compare existing nanobodies, enter the target and each full VHH sequence.
Give every candidate a unique FASTA name.

23
00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:44.600
One candidate produced four results, one per engine.
The Boltz-2 ipSAE is 0.378. Check each engine's scores separately.

24
00:03:44.625 --> 00:03:55.142
Read the 3D interface and its scores together.
Binding and affinity require experimental measurements.

25
00:03:55.167 --> 00:04:07.017
Enter the target and the original VHH, then check the variant settings.
The original sequence, labeled WT, is your reference.

26
00:04:07.042 --> 00:04:17.850
Set the evaluation limit to one variant and include WT.
Before running, look for one variant plus WT, each with four engines.

27
00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:27.100
WT and N100R produced eight models across four engines.
N100R replaces asparagine (N) at position 100 with arginine (R).

28
00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:37.933
Boltz-2 ipSAE is 0.378 for WT and 0.013 for N100R.
An affinity change would need to be measured experimentally.

29
00:04:37.958 --> 00:04:49.225
Completed web runs appear in Results database automatically. To add an older run,
go to Explore results, enter its workspace path and click Open existing result.

30
00:04:49.250 --> 00:05:00.975
In Results database, enter part of the run name or ID and click Search.
Click the row for public-complex to open its report in a new tab.

31
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:11.058
Choose Shareable report ZIP, then Export.
You can also save the candidate table or individual structure files.

32
00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:21.225
Extract the whole ZIP and open report.html in a browser.
Collaborators can explore the structure and results without installing NanoCoFold.
